# AHS user bottle — layered muguet F240 N60 addition study

**Date:** 2026-09-07  
**Claim mode:** named_reference  
**Reference contract:** chanel_allure_homme_sport_edt_reference_pending  
**Reference scope:** architecture  
**Family:** fresh woody aquatic / citrus-aromatic / soft tonka musk  
**Intent:** BATCH_RESCUE proposal; no physical event committed  
**Canonical record:** records/AHS_UserBottle_MuguetLayered_20260907.json  
**Immediate parent:** AHS_UserBottle_DHM200_30mL_20260907.md

**Status:** PROPOSED ADD-ONLY BENCH STUDY / NOT EXECUTED / SENSORY NOT TESTED / SAFETY AND RELEASE HOLD

## Positive additions only

For the untouched user-reported 30.000 mL parent: **Florol neat 240 microlitres (0.240 mL)** plus **Nympheal neat 60 microlitres (0.060 mL)**. Nominal final volume: **30.300 mL**. The [addition-only card](AHS_MuguetLayered_AddOnly_CARD_20260907.md) gives the isolated sample scale. Do not change the whole bottle automatically.

No additional Mayol, Helional, DHM, Hedione, Calone, musk, wood, salicylate, carrier or ethanol. This is an alternative to the Mayol-only proposal, not a stacked second correction. No Mayol addition was reported; if the bottle has changed, this parent no longer applies.

## Layering and chosen trial spacing

Florol is the main added soft muguet petal body; Nympheal a smaller watery-floral density/definition role. Existing Helional supplies green/cyclamen/ozonic contour, Hedione the transparent floral connection, and existing salicylate/methylionone/woods/musks the drydown connection. Roles and nonredundancy are hypotheses, not observed results. Nympheal is not assumed to be a separate fast top note.

The 4:1 supplied-stock-volume ratio is a perfumer-designed test, not a mass/OAV ratio, a literature optimum or recovered Chanel proportions. Total addition is 1% of the initial nominal bottle volume; the 40/10 microlitre sample transfers meet the 10 microlitre floor without a new carrier. No promise of immediate punch is made.

Mayol remains a separate alternative. More Helional/DHM/Calone would alter the retained freshness axes; Bourgeonal20%TEC has unresolved fraction basis; Cyclamen adds another green-aldehydic axis; FreesiaHDI/LilyrealND have composition uncertainty. Hydroxycitronellol is not Hydroxycitronellal. No Lilial, additional musk/fixative, sweet material or natural is added.

